  "description": "<p>Concordia University Chicago is a private university in River Forest, Illinois. Over 100 courses in varied subjects are available for students enrolled at Concordia University Chicago. The University attracts around 216 international students from different countries annually. The institution is just 10 miles from the centre of Chicago in a prime location.</p><h2>What is the Concordia University Chicago acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Concordia University Chicago acceptance rate is 88%.</p> <p>The University boasts impressive facilities such as academic buildings, Christopher Center for Library and Information Resources, Black Box Theatre, and more. Several athletic facilities, including the Geiseman Gymnasium, Concordia Stadium, and Physical Fitness Center, are also available, with a swimming pool, weight room, and cardio equipment. Impressively, the Main Dining Room on campus serves all-you-can-eat meals. The Chapel Cafe and Student Union Cafe are also convenient locations for students to grab a bite to eat on campus.</p><p>Religious students can find a place to pray and worship on campus at the Chapel of the Lord. Students can also benefit from mental health and medical services, including health checks and counseling.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The Campus Activities Board (CAB) is an interdependent student-led organization that creates communities by promoting fun and impactful events. All students are welcome to join the activities organised on campus. Students have a variety of student clubs to choose from to meet like-minded people, from an art club to a cooking club, a swing dance club to women in engineering, and other organizations. The Office of Multicultural Student Engagement aims to encourage an inclusive environment to continue to grow on campus.</p>",
